-- title:
--   Extending a valuation ring of F₁ to a place of F/L
-- statement:
--   Let $k_0$, $L$, $F$ be fields with $L$ and $F$ algebras over $k_0$ and $F$ an algebra over $L$, the three structures forming a scalar tower; let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $F/k_0$ and $K_1$ an intermediate field of $L/k_0$, and write $F_1 := k_0(\,\mathrm{im}(K_1 \to F)\,) \sqcup F_0$ for the intermediate field of $F/k_0$ generated by the image of $K_1$ in $F$ together with $F_0$. Assume: (i) $k_0(\,\mathrm{im}(L \to F)\,) \sqcup F_0 = F$; (ii) for every $n$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to L$ that is linearly independent over $K_1$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to F$ with all $a_i \in F_1$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ in $F$ (images of the $c_i$ taken in $F$) forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$; (iii) every valuation subring $O$ of $F$ that contains the image of $L$ and satisfies $O \neq F$ is a principal ideal ring. Let $V_1$ be a valuation subring of $F_1$ with $V_1 \neq F_1$ containing the image in $F_1$ of every element of $K_1$ that lands in $F_1$. Then there is a place $P$ of $F$ over $L$, that is, a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $L$, different from $F$ and a principal ideal ring, such that an element of $F_1$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ exactly when it lies in $V_1$; that is, $\mathcal{O}_P \cap F_1 = V_1$.
--
--   This is Chevalley's place-extension theorem in the shape required for a tower of constant fields: a non-trivial valuation ring of the level field $F_1$, compatible with $K_1$, is the restriction of a place of $F$ trivial on $L$, the linear disjointness hypothesis (ii) guaranteeing that the ideal generated by the maximal ideal of $V_1$ in the compositum with $L$ stays proper. It is used in the construction of regular prolongations, where it supplies a place at which prescribed evaluations vanish to the order given by divisibility by a prime.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_exists_forall_mem_iff_adjoin_sup_of_linearDisjoint.lean

